BUILD_EXIT=0 TEST_EXIT=0 (MarkerClusterModelTest=11, MarkerClusterDiagnosticsTest=3 -> 14 new tests pass; full :android release unit suite green) LINT_EXIT=0 (ktlintCheck main+test+androidTest + detekt warningsAsErrors) PLACEHOLDER_EXIT=0 (PLACEHOLDER_COUNT=0).
Surface: com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/MarkerCluster (MarkerCluster.kt view + MarkerClusterModel.kt model) -- native parity port of web components/maps/MarkerCluster.tsx. The web source is a headless leaflet primitive (takes a points prop, registers a markercluster group via useMap, returns null); the native surface is the self-contained TeslaMap region a feature drops in: radius-aware clustering over the shared unit-tested clusterMarkers grid, density bubbles (clusterColor thresholds 100/25/10), singleton dot markers (VehicleMarker) with popup + ORIGINAL-point click forwarding, the 5000-point cap applied before the finite-coordinate filter, a MapAccessibleSummary screen-reader list, a friendly empty state, and the one-shot PII-safe view.opened slug=MarkerCluster (P1/S11).
Data binding: the only web hook is useMap (the leaflet map context, not a network query), so -- like the committed RouteDisplay precedent -- the surface is prop-driven with no Source/ViewModel; inventing a P1/S8 state holder would drift from the spec. i18n uses existing P1/S10 catalog keys (mapOverview_locations, mapOverview_noLocation); the web source declares no i18n keys.
NOTE: the gate runs :android: (settings.gradle.kts maps the prompt's :app: -> the :android module).
NOTE: MarkerClusterUiTest.kt (androidTest) ktlint-passes and is the on-emulator UI/a11y/diagnostics spec; it mirrors the committed precedent RouteDisplayUiTest verbatim. The androidTest source set has a PRE-EXISTING, repo-wide compile gap (compose-ui-test assertExists/assertDoesNotExist/onAllNodes unresolved) that is byte-identical for ALL sibling UI tests including the gate-passed RouteDisplayUiTest.kt:4:33. It is NOT part of the per-surface gate (which never compiles androidTest) and a fix would require an androidTest build.gradle dependency change outside this artifact's allowed files. The pure projection + diagnostics that back every UI state are covered off-device by the passing :android:testReleaseUnitTest suite above.

